//? Title: Non-Local Attention: Four Affinities, Global Derivatives and Explicit Fitting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Non-local blocks mix every query with all key/value positions. We compare four affinity
rules and both pooling modes against a dense tensor composition, inspect global derivative
support, then visibly optimize a complete five-module compact ResNet-50.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.5_attention_and_modern_convnets/non_local.cpp`.

> The method

With P=H*W queries, M keys and inner width floor(C/2), the response is y=A*g, followed by
biased pointwise projection, learned BN (epsilon 1e-5) and the raw input shortcut. Pairwise
modes differ in both affinity and normalization: embedded Gaussian uses softmax(theta*phiᵀ/
sqrt(inner)), Gaussian uses softmax(x*x_keyᵀ) without embeddings, dot product uses
(theta*phiᵀ)/M, and concatenation uses ReLU(theta*w1+(phi*w2)ᵀ)/M. Only the Gaussian rows
are probability distributions. Dot weights can be signed; concatenation rows do not generally
sum to one. The query/key matrix costs O(NPM*inner) arithmetic and O(NPM) storage.

The source's subsampling convention max-pools INPUT features by 2×2 VALID before applying
key/value projections. That is not generally equivalent to max-pooling phi/g after projection.
The code preserves and explicitly checks that source convention, including odd-side VALID
flooring. M then becomes floor(H/2)*floor(W/2). Projected g/theta/phi/W filters are biased
He-uniform; the embedded-Gaussian scale follows the source release adaptation. No learned
attention is detached: derivatives flow through affinities, normalization, values and output.

Output BN gamma starts at zero, so a new block is exact signed identity with identity input
derivatives; interior attention parameter gradients can initially be zero until the gate opens.
Active no-pooling Gaussian/embedded/dot fixtures show one output depending on every input
position, unlike a local 3×3 filter. Max pooling and concatenation ReLU can select fewer paths.
The support probe uses saved BN values to isolate attention from training BN's global coupling.

The backbone retains all sixteen ResNet-50 bottlenecks. It attaches non-local modules after
zero-based blocks 0/2 in stage two and 0/2/4 in stage three: five total for depth 50. A deeper
backbone would select more even-index blocks. Full width adds 7358464 scalars to plain ResNet-50,
for 32915496 learned scalars. The 64-pixel full-width count/backward probe activates non-local
gamma and freezes moving updates in BOTH the backbone and captured hook. It retains all
channels/blocks but is not an ImageNet-resolution benchmark. Some biases have true training
invariances: phi shifts softmax rows; g and W shifts become constants removed by BN. Finite
gradients are checked without requiring every tensor to have a nonzero derivative.

The explicit fit uses quarter widths, a 3×3 stride-one stem without pooling, stage stride on
the first 1×1 and all sixteen backbone blocks plus five embedded-Gaussian modules. It has
1947546 learned/15328 moving scalars. Non-local maps are 16×16 and 8×8 with key/value
subsampling. All preprocessing, augmentation, model, loss and update computations use tensors.
The loop shows 128 fit/64 validation/64 official-test original CIFAR images, four batch-eight
epochs (64 updates, kept short for build time), Adam(.001), explicit kernel L2=.0001/2, padded crops/flips and paired learned/BN
validation checkpoints. This small single-seed fit cannot establish an attention accuracy or
latency advantage and does not reproduce the source's larger training schedule.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/non_local_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/non_local_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/non_local_concept.tikz > build/non_local_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/non_local_concept.svg build/non_local_concept.dvi > build/non_local_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
